      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that the value of $x$ is one-half the value of $y$, we can write this relationship as:\n\\[ x = \\frac{1}{2}y \\]\n\nNext, we know that the value of $y$ is one-fifth the value of $z$. We are given that $z = 60$. Therefore, we can express this relationship as:\n\\[ y = \\frac{1}{5}z \\]\nSubstituting the value of $z$ into the equation, we get:\n\\[ y = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 60 = 12 \\]\n\nNow that we have the value of $y$, we can substitute it back into the equation for $x$:\n\\[ x = \\frac{1}{2}y = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the value of $x$ is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]",
